{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"An ETF’s expense ratio is collected **from the fund’s assets—not as a separate charge to your brokerage account**.\n\n- The fund generally accrues expenses daily, reducing its net asset value (NAV). It periodically pays those expenses from fund assets.\n- Those costs are already reflected in the ETF’s NAV and reported returns. You don’t lose shares or receive a separate bill.\n- For example, a **0.20% annual expense ratio** costs approximately **$20 per year on an average $10,000 investment**. Your actual cost varies with your investment’s value and holding period.\n\n**Worth knowing:** Brokerage commissions, bid–ask spreads, and certain fund trading costs are separate from the expense ratio."}}
